ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":96,"prev":98,"next":101,"titles":103,"firmware":272},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":28,"procedures":58,"parameters":75,"related":76,"body":81,"sources":82,"official_url":32,"controls":89},"com.system-settings","System settings",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"settings","system menu","preferences","brightness","power-off type","date and time","detune","com",10,"knowledge/manual/units/com/system-settings.md",{"modes":16,"screens":17},[],[18],"system settings","Device-wide options behind `com → M1`, in sections: system (brightness, country, power-off), keyboard (velocity, detune), midi, clock, pitchbend calibration, battery and the MIDI monitor. OS 1.2 drops the keyboard section: see the OS 1.2 unit.","outdated-in-guide",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[24,25],"1.1.17","1.2.0","1.1.15",null,[29,34,37,40,45,48,51,54],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"navigate","In the system settings `E1` picks a section, `E2` a setting within it and `E3` (or `E4`) its value; `M1` goes back to the com page.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/com#system-settings","official",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"system","The system section holds screen brightness, LED brightness, country and whether switching off happens at once or after a delay, which guards against powering down by accident mid-performance.",{"id":38,"text":39,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"keyboard","Up to OS 1.1.33 the keyboard section sets how the built-in keys respond to velocity and can detune them, by notes and by cents, for microtonal scales.",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":43,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":27,"confidence":44},"keyboard-os12","On OS 1.2 the keyboard section is gone; its velocity choice is the system section's last row, and the sections are system, midi, clock, pitchbend, battery, usb, monitor and legal.","docs/research/79b-os12-small-features.md#3-com--system-page-120","community-verified",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"clock","The clock section holds the date and time that the unit stamps on snapshots, autosaves and project versions.",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"pitchbend","The pitchbend section calibrates the strip — `E2` sets the sensitivity of its left side, `E3` of its right side, and `M4` runs the calibration.",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"battery","The battery section shows the charge level and the input current limit.",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":57,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"sample-preview","OS 1.1.17 added a system setting for sample preview, which the guide does not list.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.17",[59],{"id":60,"goal":61,"preconditions":62,"steps":63,"result":27,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"calibrate-pitchbend","Calibrate the pitchbend strip",[],[64,66,69,72],{"keys":65,"note":27,"set":27},"com → M1",{"keys":67,"note":68,"set":27},"turn E1","pitchbend section",{"keys":70,"note":71,"set":27},"turn E2/E3","left and right sensitivity",{"keys":73,"note":74,"set":27},"M4","starts the calibration; follow the screen",[],[77,78,79,80],"com.system-settings-os12","com.midi-settings","com.midi-monitor","howto.enable-velocity","Most options here are set once: brightness, country, the date used to stamp files and how the unit\npowers off. Two sections matter for playing — keyboard, where velocity is switched on and keys can\nbe detuned, and pitchbend, where you recalibrate the strip when bends feel lopsided. The midi and\nmonitor sections have units of their own.",[83,85,87],{"url":32,"kind":84},"guide",{"url":43,"kind":86},